---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { formatDate, isoDate } from '../lib/utils';

const crumbs = [
	{ label: 'Home', href: '/' },
	{ label: 'Affiliate Disclosure', href: '/affiliate-disclosure/' },
];

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-06-20');
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Affiliate Disclosure"
	description="Exactly how GutWise makes money, which affiliate programmes we belong to, and the rules we follow so commission never shapes a recommendation. Read more."
	schemaNodes={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}
>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="Legal"
		title="How GutWise makes money"
		intro="Stated in full, because a recommendation you cannot audit is worth very little."
		crumbs={crumbs}
	/>

	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
		<p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
			Last updated{' '}
			<time datetime={isoDate(lastUpdated)}>{formatDate(lastUpdated)}</time>
		</p>

		<div class="prose prose-gutwise mt-8">
			<h2>The short version</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE.name} is reader-supported. Some links on this site are affiliate
				links, which means that if you click one and buy something, we may earn a
				small commission. <strong>It costs you nothing extra</strong> — the price
				is the same as it would have been.
			</p>

			<h2>Our rules</h2>
			<p>These are the commitments we hold ourselves to.</p>

			<h3>Commission never determines placement</h3>
			<p>
				We decide what to recommend and in what order before checking whether
				anything pays a commission. The clearest evidence is our most-recommended
				product overall — the Monash University FODMAP app — which has no
				affiliate programme and earns us nothing at all. It is still first on the
				list, because it is the right answer.
			</p>

			<h3>We tell you when not to buy</h3>
			<p>
				Most of a low-FODMAP diet is ordinary supermarket food. Where a specialty
				product is an unnecessary premium, we say so on the page, even though
				recommending it would pay better. Our pantry guide exists mainly to argue
				you out of buying thirty things.
			</p>

			<h3>Disclosure appears before the links</h3>
			<p>
				Every page carrying affiliate links shows a disclosure above the fold and
				before the first link, in line with the US Federal Trade Commission's
				requirement that disclosures be clear and conspicuous. A disclosure buried
				in a footer does not meet that standard, and we do not rely on one.
			</p>

			<h3>We do not accept paid placement</h3>
			<p>
				No brand can buy a position on this site, and we do not publish sponsored
				posts dressed up as editorial. If that ever changes, any such content will
				be labelled unmistakably as advertising.
			</p>

			<h2>Programmes we participate in</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Amazon Associates.</strong> {SITE.name} is a participant in the
					Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program
					designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by
					advertising and linking to Amazon.com. Amazon and the Amazon logo are
					trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Specialty low-FODMAP brands.</strong> We take part in affiliate
					programmes run by certified low-FODMAP food brands where we already
					recommend the product on its merits.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Display advertising.</strong> Once a page meets the traffic
					threshold required to qualify, we may show display advertising. Ad
					placements are never editorial recommendations.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>How affiliate links are marked</h2>
			<p>
				Affiliate links carry <code>rel="nofollow sponsored"</code> attributes, so
				they are machine-identifiable as commercial links as well as disclosed to
				you in plain language.
			</p>

			<h2>What we earn and what we know about you</h2>
			<p>
				Retailers report commissions to us in aggregate. We are told that a number
				of purchases were attributed to us; we are not told who made them or what
				else was in the basket. Tracking is done by the retailer's own cookie
				under their privacy policy, not ours. See our{' '}
				<a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how that interacts with
				the rest of the site.
			</p>

			<h2>Questions</h2>
			<p>
				If you think a recommendation on this site looks commercially motivated,
				tell us. Email{' '}
				<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will explain the
				reasoning or change the page. {SITE.responseTimePromise}
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
